    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present No. 14 Griffith Road, a charming and well-proportioned three-bedroom mid-terrace family home ideally positioned within this mature and established residential location in Finglas. Extending to approximately 68 sqm, this property offers bright and practical accommodation throughout and represents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, young families or investors alike.\n\nOn entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright entrance hallway which leads into the spacious living room. The living room benefits from a feature open fireplace, creating a warm and inviting focal point. To the rear is a well-proportioned kitchen with direct access to the property's impressive rear garden. A ground floor family bathroom, complete with both bath and shower, is also located downstairs.\n\nUpstairs comprises three well-appointed bedrooms, including two generous double bedrooms and a good-sized single bedroom. The property benefits from double glazing throughout and gas-fired central heating.\n\nOne of the standout features of No. 14 is the large south-easterly facing rear garden, which offers excellent natural light and provides a fantastic outdoor space for relaxing, entertaining or family use. The garden also benefits from a substantial block-built shed, ideal for additional storage and fully plumbed for a washing machine.\n\nSituated in a mature residential setting, No. 14 Griffith Road is within walking distance of local bus stops, providing regular services to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. Finglas Village, Glasnevin and Charlestown Shopping Centre are all within easy reach, offering a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. The property is also ideally positioned for access to a fantastic selection of recreational facilities, including Johnstown Park, Albert College Park and the National Botanic Gardens, while a host of local sporting clubs and leisure facilities are also nearby. For commuters, the M50 Motorway is just minutes away, providing easy access to Dublin's northside and all major national routes. Dublin Airport is also within approximately 15 minutes' drive, while DCU and IKEA are both conveniently accessible.\n\nViewing is highly recommended. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 015411455 or 0861985247 to arrange a viewing or for further information.\n\nAdditional Features\n• C. 68 sqm\n• BER C\n• Built 1957\n• Three-bedroom mid-terrace family home\n• Two generous double bedrooms\n• One good-sized single bedroom\n• Bright entrance hallway\n• Spacious living room\n• Feature open fireplace\n• Kitchen to rear\n• Ground floor family bathroom\n• Bath and shower facilities\n• Large south-easterly facing rear garden\n• Block-built shed\n• Shed fully plumbed for washing machine\n• Double glazing throughout\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Local bus stops within walking distance\n• Excellent public transport links\n• M50 Motorway within minutes' drive\n• Approximately 15 minutes from Dublin Airport\n• Close to Finglas Village, Glasnevin and Charlestown Shopping Centre\n• Easy access to DCU and IKEA\n• Close to Johnstown Park, Albert College Park and National Botanic Gardens\n• Excellent selection of schools and local amenities nearby\n• Ideal for first-time buyers, families and investors"
      },
